Give every second dispatch cell of a run its own cell-info entry (MaxCellInfoLookupDistance 100 -> 2).

ILC sorts dispatch cells by target method and stores the (interface, slot) info only for every 100th
cell of a run; the runtime finds a cell's info by stepping back to the previous entry, and every step is
a full NativeArray.TryGetAt descent - ~5 failed lookups per resolution in the Nethermind guest. With a
distance of 2 a lookup fails at most once. 1 is not possible without changing VertexArray: it would put
one unified vertex in both slots of a pair, and the pair encoding needs its second vertex placed after
the pair, while a unified vertex is placed only once (the first time). With 2, two entries are adjacent
only across a run boundary, as before, so each vertex is still placed at most once.

The info table grows by about 2 bytes per cell (+4 KiB ELF for the Nethermind guest's ~1,160 cells).

Nethermind stateless guest on ZisK (ziskemu 1.3.0), on top of perf-73: ~250 steps less per resolution.
  block 26055159 steps 55,823,836 -> 55,739,060 (-0.15%)
  block 26112793 steps 130,833,026 -> 130,744,346 (-0.07%)
Outputs identical on 11 mainnet blocks.

